Here's the full resolution, condensed, with the LaunchDaemon files included.

**Root cause:** The Thunderbolt Bridge virtual interface (`bridge0`) on the 2018 MacBook Pro was stuck in a broken STP/learning state, blocking all traffic between the Macs, even though the physical Thunderbolt link itself was healthy (confirmed via `system_profiler SPThunderboltDataType`, which showed a clean 40 Gb/s connection).

**Steps that led to the fix:**

1. Pings failed with "No route to host" / "Host is down" over Thunderbolt Bridge.
2. `ifconfig bridge0` showed member ports stuck at `flags=3<LEARNING,DISCOVER>`, never reaching forwarding state.
3. Ruled out the cable (worked fine with a different MacBook Air) and ruled out Pro hardware (SMC reset, port swap, display test, and finally `system_profiler` confirmed a healthy 40 Gb/s link).
4. Also fixed a malformed subnet mask along the way (`255.255.0.0.0` → `255.255.0.0`).
5. Since the bridge layer itself was the problem, we bypassed it: matched each Mac's live Thunderbolt MAC to its physical interface using `networksetup -listallhardwareports`:
   - Air → Thunderbolt 2 → `en2`
   - Pro → Thunderbolt 3 → `en3`
6. Deleted the Thunderbolt Bridge network service on both Macs, then assigned static IPs directly to the physical interfaces:
```
sudo ifconfig en2 inet 10.0.0.1 netmask 255.255.0.0 up   # Air
sudo ifconfig en3 inet 10.0.0.2 netmask 255.255.0.0 up   # Pro
```
This worked immediately — 0% packet loss, ~1.2ms latency.

**Making it permanent (LaunchDaemons):**

Since `ifconfig` settings don't survive reboot, we created a LaunchDaemon on each Mac to reapply the IP automatically at boot.

`com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.air.plist` (Air):
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.air</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/sbin/ifconfig</string>
        <string>en2</string>
        <string>inet</string>
        <string>10.0.0.1</string>
        <string>netmask</string>
        <string>255.255.0.0</string>
        <string>up</string>
    </array>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/thunderbolt-ip.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/thunderbolt-ip.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
```

`com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.pro.plist` (Pro):
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.pro</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/sbin/ifconfig</string>
        <string>en3</string>
        <string>inet</string>
        <string>10.0.0.2</string>
        <string>netmask</string>
        <string>255.255.0.0</string>
        <string>up</string>
    </array>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/thunderbolt-ip.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/thunderbolt-ip.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
```

**Install commands (run on each Mac with its own plist):**
```
sudo mv ~/Downloads/com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.air.plist /Library/LaunchDaemons/
sudo chown root:wheel /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.air.plist
sudo chmod 644 /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.air.plist
sudo launchctl load /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.hope.thunderbolt-ip.air.plist
```
(swap filename/interface/IP for the Pro's version)

**Note:** if you ever move the cable to a different Thunderbolt port, the `enX` name may shift and the daemon will need updating — check with `networksetup -listallhardwareports` again if connectivity drops after a future reboot.
